Release C SDK 0.8.0 with an experimental lock provider role

The lock provider contract (sophia-lock-files-v1.kdl, sophia-lock-files.md
and its golden records) was imported unmodified from Sophia fd6ea7538. It is
byte-identical at Sophia's signed master merge
61d545c9087a685c5161f0d5f3132436aa82d31e, which this release names as its
contract revision. Every other spec copy also matches that master. The
copied contract still marks itself revision 1 (draft), so the lock API is
experimental until Sophia accepts it explicitly.

The release adds sophia_lock_files.h (sophia_lf_*, the record codec) and
sophia_lock_client.h (sophia_lc_*, a nonblocking provider client). No
existing header, structure or symbol changes. struct sophia_lc_client holds
the 9P client by pointer, embeds the existing sophia_9p_handle in its
operation slots, and otherwise embeds new lock record types.

compatibility.json declares lock_files false until the contract is accepted
and Sophia's permanent production lock export harness passes with this
release vendored. Upload pipelining remains a follow-up.
